ls": 1, "ended_on_rejection": false, "error": null, "exec_mode": "local", "failure_class": "solved", "failure_reason": null, "faults_served": 0, "final_answer_complete": true, "final_answer_present": true, "final_answer_source": "json", "final_workspace": "/workspace/openbench-ab/results/omp-screen5-b2/omp-35/omp-35/cells/without/trig-omp-multistep/3/workspace", "fresh_subagents": 0, "harness": "omp", "harness_version": "omp/17.3.4 (/workspace/pi-check/cache5/bin/omp/5441679975d80bf1d7609159f23ef383336e8a9b/omp)", "harness_version_source": "host", "host": "grok-bot-vm-412615941", "image_digest": null, "last_activity_age_s": null, "list_has_generated": null, "main_agent_searched": false, "model": "claude-opus-5-5", "model_context_window": 1000000, "model_max_tokens": 128000, "output_tail": "Root cause: `to_cents` truncates float error \u2014 `19.99 * 100 == 1998.9999\u2026` \u2192 `int()` gives `1998`. Same for `0.29` and `4.35`.\n`Decimal(str(amount))` uses the shortest decimal representation (`\"19.99\"`), so float representation error never reaches the rounding step. pytest isn't installed; running the tests directly:\nI fixed the bug in `ledger/currency.py`. All four tests in `tests/test_totals.py` now pass, and so does `tests/test_report.py`. pytest isn't installed here, so I ran the test functions directly with a small Python loop rather than through pytest.\n\n**Cause:** `to_cents` did `int(amount * 100)`, which cuts off the decimal part instead of rounding. Floats can't store most prices exactly, so `19.99 * 100` comes out as `1998.9999\u2026` and became `1998`. The same thing happened with `0.29` and `4.35`. The wrong subtotals then carried through to the tax and discount totals.\n\n**Fix:** `to_cents` now converts the amount to a `Decimal` via `str(amount)`, multiplies by 100, and rounds half-up to a whole cent. That matches the half-up rounding `discounts.py` and `tax.py` already use. Going through `str()` avoids the float error because it gives `\"19.99\"